WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Three designs, one governed study.
The scientist supplies candidate meshes, flight conditions and the rules for a valid design freeze.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Execute the full CFD matrix.
The agent drives SU2 for every candidate–condition pair and retains the numerical outputs.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Keep the failed candidate visible.
K42 exceeds the crossload and pressure recovery limits. K17 and K88 remain feasible across the study.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Trace all 414 iterations.
Inspect the native certification history for K17 at CROSS_12. The log pressure residual reaches −8.010.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Freeze K17 for prototyping.
The selected design stays within all four limits. The delivered package links the decision to its configuration, mesh and solver outputs.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Start from the supplied claims.
Five workloads and five approximation degrees define the study. Calibration data and a reproduction profile establish the comparison.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Rebuild the compilation evidence.
The agent produces native Qiskit and Cirq artifacts and records gate count, depth, infidelity, duration and estimated success.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Less circuit cost, more error.
Each workload is evaluated from exact synthesis to stronger approximation. The reproduced values expose the fidelity trade-off.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Three mismatches remain.
One process infidelity value, one circuit depth and one qualification flag disagree with the supplied claims.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Report a claim that does not reproduce.
The final verdict preserves the discrepancies and links them to the native circuit evidence and complete comparison tables.
